        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Routine maintenance is <strong class="text-white">$15 to $40 a year</strong> and about an
            hour of your time. The failures it prevents are $300 to $800 each. Budget a further
            $250 to $500 around year seven for a belt and deck, which is wear rather than failure.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When something major does go, repair if the cost is under half the machine's replacement
            value and it is not past the midpoint of its life. And remember that a
            <a href="/best-treadmills-without-subscriptions/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">subscription</a>
            costs more over ten years than every maintenance and repair figure on this page
            combined.
          </p>
        </div>
